{"author":{"id":"a51b5961cc6de343a64125d8eb6a0f965aa434020b9c46ed932a1bbf143eb532"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791727863,"nonce":"YOzyWenoh9iESE7Kz1FgSAtBi3Y=","title":"::before and ::after with content","message":"Pseudo-elements are rejected. Owned parts with classes (.marker, .placeholder, .bar, .caret) stand in for built-ins, but authors cannot add generated content: icons, quotes, counters, decorative bars.\n\nWhere: the cascade must match ::before/::after rules to a host-made owned child at each end of an element, created when a rule with content other than none applies and destroyed when none does; content: \"text\", attr(x) and url() first, counters later. ::placeholder and ::marker could then map onto the existing parts.\n\nThe other SDK lacks it too.\n\nTests: ::before text and ::after icon; hover changes them; content: none removes; they take inherited styles; destroyed with their element (native-destroy).","files":null}]}